---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';

const EMAIL = 'support@sisrallc.com';
---

<Base
  title="Contact & Corrections"
  description="Report an error, suggest a topic, or ask a question about Wellness Med Care. We fix mistakes fast and credit the catch."
>
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:2.5rem">
    <div class="prose prose-center">
      <h1>Contact us</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Found a mistake? That is the email we answer fastest. Everything on this site is
        checked against primary sources, and when we are wrong anyway, we want to know
        the same day.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If a number, a deadline, a rule, or an explanation on this site is wrong or out
        of date, email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=Correction`}>{EMAIL}</a> with
        "Correction" in the subject line, the page address, and what you believe is
        incorrect. A link to a source helps but is not
        required. Corrections are made quickly, and the page's "current as of" date is
        updated when they are.
      </p>

      <h2>Suggestions and everything else</h2>
      <p>
        Topic requests, a tracker you wish existed, a letter template we should add, or
        anything else: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. We read everything, and
        the roadmap genuinely moves based on what people ask for.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about your data, or requests under a privacy law:
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=Privacy request`}>{EMAIL}</a>, with "Privacy
        request" in the subject line. Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>
        describes the little we collect.
      </p>

      <Callout tone="warn" title="What we cannot answer">
        <p style="margin:0">
          We cannot answer questions about your health, your symptoms, your test results,
          or your treatment - not because we do not care, but because we are not
          clinicians and answering would be harmful pretending. Those questions belong to
          a licensed clinician who can actually see your chart. If you are in a medical
          emergency, call 911.
        </p>
      </Callout>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <p>
        This site is run by a very small team. We aim to answer corrections within a day
        or two and everything else within a week. There is no phone number, and we do not
        do sales calls, link exchanges, or paid placement - please do not ask.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
